Subject: [PATCH] UI/UX polish pass: dark/gold styling, larger inputs, results
 screen, no detective
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Implements the approved dark/gold visual direction and flow within the
existing native (code-built) UI system -- no new layout framework, no
new colors introduced (colors.xml already matched the brief exactly:
near-black background, charcoal cards, gold accent, warm off-white
text). This is a styling/flow pass, not another gameplay redesign --
the voting/elimination mechanic, character architecture, and evidence
system are all untouched.

Removed old mechanics from the active flow (per section 13):
- GameManager.java: removed assignInvestigationRoles()/detective()
  (nothing ever set the detective role's UI panel visible except that
  assignment, so this is a real removal, not just hiding it).
- Player.java: removed the now-unused `detective` field.
- MainActivity.java: removed investigation()/investigationResult()/
  showCurrentRound() -- these were already unreachable dead code (no
  button ever called them), now deleted outright; removed the
  "detective" bonus panel from roleReveal(). InvestigationData/
  Story.investigation are left as inert unused internal state per the
  "old fields may remain internally" allowance, rather than touching
  Story.java's generator again for a class nothing calls anymore.

Visual polish (applies everywhere via the shared helpers, not a
per-screen rewrite):
- addPanel(): panels now have a subtle gold-toned border stroke for a
  defined "card" edge, corner radius 12->14dp.
- button(): corner radius 12->14dp, height 56->58dp.
- Player name input fields (the explicitly reported "small/clipped"
  ones): height 52->64dp, real vertical padding (was 0), text size
  18->19sp, more breathing room between fields (8dp->12dp gaps).
- Custom-story text fields: same height/padding increase; multi-line
  fields now align text to top-start instead of center (center-aligned
  multi-line text visibly jumps around while typing -- a real bug fix,
  not just a style tweak).

Flow/copy changes to match the specified screens:
- Story introduction: title is now "القصة: <name>", continue button
  is "متابعة" (was "إعداد اللاعبين").
- Free discussion: title "وقت النقاش" (was "نقاش حر"), now recap the
  case (story title + the incident line from the introduction) before
  the discussion controls.
- Voting: added an explicit confirm step (confirmVote()) between
  picking a target and the vote being recorded, so a mistap can't
  silently lock in the wrong accusation -- "تأكيد التصويت" /
  "تغيير الاختيار".
- Reveal: restructured to the specified order -- title "الحقيقة",
  then the guilty character name(s) with "كان/كانوا المذنبين" stated
  plainly, then the full role list, then the solution/ending text.
- Added a dedicated results() screen after reveal(): win/loss banner,
  guilty character name(s), rounds played, wrong-vote count (all from
  data GameManager already tracked -- no new scoring mechanic), with
  "العب مرة أخرى" (restarts the same story with the same player names)
  and "اختر قصة أخرى" buttons.

strings.xml:
- voting: "التصويت" -> "حان وقت التصويت" (matches spec exactly).
- Removed your_secret/your_statement/back_to_stories -- genuinely
  unused now, not just hidden.
- discussion and instructions strings referenced the removed
  secret/statement mechanic ("اقرؤوا جملكم"، "دوره وسره") -- left over
  from an earlier phase and no longer accurate. Fixed the wording to
  describe what's actually there now (this is a correctness fix for
  leftover dead-mechanic copy, not new/changed game content).

Verified: full javac compile against the same Android/org.json API
stub set used throughout this project (0 errors), 14/14 JUnit tests
unaffected and passing, and the 13-story data/logic smoke test still
passes (nothing about story content or the character/evidence
architecture was touched in this pass).

Known limitations (native app, no visual preview available in this
environment, no image generation used per instructions):
- Story cards are still single-column stacked panels, not the
  photographic hero-image cards shown in the mockup -- there's no
  artwork pipeline in this project to source per-story images from.
- I could not visually render the app to confirm final pixel-level
  spacing/typography against the mockup; changes were verified by
  code review and compilation, not a rendered screenshot.
- The underlying voting mechanic is still per-round elimination
  (matches the existing, tested system) rather than a single
  simultaneous vote-then-reveal, per the explicit instruction not to
  redesign the game mechanic again.
